  "schema": "arcpuzzles-parametric-prototype-evidence-v1",
  "scope": "# Review: d5a059b0f3a6 conflicted-return reconciliation\n\nStatus: **routine focused repair; no production-generator or canonical-rule change**.\nGenerator version `3.1.0`; generator SHA-256 `8276303d89c43e360a4990344a3ccf04a0321e0b490aaa4300c36e3d0c86975d`; canonical rule hash `77f0ca66f33e`.\nDefect: public challenge names were content-derived, but `verify.py` wrote them immediately in private `ALLOWED_SETTINGS` order, exposing a setting-associated creation-order channel.\nRepair: retain the current prototype, stage and redact all public challenges first, reject duplicate visible identifiers, then emit them in lexicographic visible-filename order.\nPreserved: independent `n_train`/`n_test`, the 3-demo/4-query default, exact canonical default program, setting-sensitive queries, and current production source.\nTDD: the reversed-private-order regression failed on the issued verifier (`1 failed, 25 passed, 18 subtests`) and passed after repair (`26 passed, 18 subtests`).\nRacket: seed `20261023` exercised two programs over seven shared inputs, for 14 exact Racket/Python checks; all four queries per episode remained setting-sensitive.\nAdversarial pass: normal/reversed private enumeration produced the same public sequence; query-output leakage, hidden seed metadata, and visible-ID collisions were rejected.\nSupplementary tickets: four-query support was bounded and the stale absolute census-path request was reproduced; neither changes variant approval or shared runtime behavior.\nNeeds attention: `both_axes` remains an unapproved finite prototype, and the checks do not prove exhaustive identifiability or absence of every storage side channel.",
  "task_id": "d5a059b0f3a6",
  "variant_approved": false,
  "verification_status": "reviewer_reported"
